nd the junction spaces and associators are the finite semisimple unitary Ising fusion data above. In particular $D_L$ is non-invertible. The claim is confined to this finite lattice model and asserts no continuum limit or empirical fact.","physical_scope":"An exact finite periodic quantum Ising spin chain and its declared finite defect-network extension at the self-dual zero-field coupling; no infinite-volume, continuum-QFT, universality, or empirical claim is made.","provenance":{"statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated"},"proof_strategy":"direct","sources":{"references":[{"title":"David Aasen, Roger S. K. Mong, and Paul Fendley, Topological Defects on the Lattice I: The Ising Model","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1601.07185","locator":"§§2–3.2, PDF pp. 3–11, for the Ising transfer/dual Hilbert spaces, duality kernel, local Pauli intertwiners and character-sum fusion; §§4.1–4.3, PDF pp. 17–22, for trivalent junctions and F-moves."},{"title":"Jürg Fröhlich, Jürgen Fuchs, Ingo Runkel, and Christoph Schweigert, Kramers–Wannier Duality from Conformal Defects","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0404051","locator":"Critical-Ising defect discussion, PDF pp. 2–5: independent CFT treatment of the duality defect and fusion rule; no continuum limit is inferred here."},{"title":"Steven H. Simon, Topological Quantum, §§9.2–9.3","url":"https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/SteveSimon/topological2020/TopoBookSep12.pdf","locator":"PDF pp. 119–121 (book pagination approximately 103–105): Ising F-symbols, mixed associators and pentagon convention."},{"title":"Nils Carqueville, Lecture Notes on 2-Dimensional Defect TQFT","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.05747","locator":"§2.1, PDF pp. 5–8: model-defined defect bordisms, junctions, isotopy classes and correlator functor; oriented 2D setting only."}]}}]},{"id":"qftx-noninvertible-symmetries-examples","items":[{"id":"ex-aqft-ising-fusion-object-noninvertible","kind":"example","domain":"mathematics","library":"physic