items/post-aqft-smeft-model.md:46:There are no right-handed neutrino fields. Fermion components are Grassmann odd; $H$ is a Grassmann-even complex doublet. The global charges are $B(q_L)=B(u_R)=B(d_R)=1/3$, $L(\ell_L)=L(e_R)=1$, and zero for $H$ and the gauge fields; the corresponding $U(1)_B$ and $U(1)_L$ transformations multiply each field by the phase determined by its charge. Impose these as exact selection rules on the retained formal local interactions; no anomaly-free quantum-current claim is made. There is no flavor symmetry beyond the displayed gauge action: Yukawa and Wilson coefficients may carry unrestricted three-family indices subject to the stated reality and Hermitian-conjugation conditions.
items/post-aqft-smeft-model.md:50:Choose the trivial smooth right principal bundle $P=M\times G_{\mathrm{SM}}$ and only this bundle sector. A connection is a smooth right-principal connection with the convention $\omega(Z_P)=Z$ and $R_g^*\omega=\operatorname{Ad}_{g^{-1}}\omega$. In a local section, a field in representation $\rho$ has covariant derivative $D_\mu=\partial_\mu+\rho_*(A_\mu)$, and the gauge curvature is $F_A=dA+\tfrac12[A\wedge A]$ with the graded-bracket convention of the supplied gauge-geometry data. The ordinary component hypercharges are $Y=y/6$; in particular $Y(H)=1/2$. The formal local interaction set imposes the exact $U(1)_B$ and $U(1)_L$ selection rules stated above; no anomaly-free quantum-current claim is made. Yukawa matrices are otherwise arbitrary.
