items/def-aqft-chiral-power-counting.md:45:The factors $(\varphi/v)^B$ and $(h/v)^{H_{\mathrm{ext}}}$ contain any number of Goldstone and singlet fields and do not increase $d_\chi$. Vertices $\varphi^{2j}h^a$ from the leading two-derivative scalar sector likewise carry no additional term in this degree formula. Here $\varphi$ denotes the local Goldstone coordinates defined by $U=\exp(2i\varphi^aT_a/v)$ in its stated coordinate chart. The chiral cutoff and loop cutoff are supplied independently; this contract retains the leading order and the one-loop next-to-leading counterterm classes with $L\leq1$ and $d_\chi\geq0$.
