items/ex-aqft-two-group-nonzero-postnikov-unit-response.md:73:4.1 By [A1], both configurations have weight $1$ and the gauge bijection fixes the unique configuration, so the partition functions agree with phase $1$. The coupling theorem [F5] yields the same relation. Thus this selected response has no anomaly phase although its background Postnikov class is nonzero; this conclusion uses the separate unit-response model input, not $\beta$ alone. [A1, F4, F5, step 3.1, algebra] ∎
