items/ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation.md:27:      locator: “Non Abelian Anomaly in 4 Dimensions,” equations (54)–(57), PDF pp. 10–11; left-minus-right chiral traces and cubic-index cancellation.
items/ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation.md:40:Let $\mathfrak g=\mathbb R t$ be the one-dimensional Abelian real Lie algebra and take $V_+=V_-=\mathbb C$. For $q\in\mathbb R$, define complex-linear representations by $\rho_\pm(zt)=\pm qz\,\operatorname{id}_{\mathbb C}$ for $z\in\mathbb C$, and attach the left-handed bookkeeping label to both. This opposite-charge pair is called vectorlike at the representation-data level here. It does not construct spinor fields or a charge-conjugation map; an interpretation as a field pair requires a separately specified field model and convention. The coefficient sums satisfy $q^3+(-q)^3=0$ and $q+(-q)=0$. With the no-half anticommutator convention $\{A,B\}=AB+BA$, the cubic coefficient is $d=2(q^3+(-q)^3)=0$, and the separate linear representation coefficient is $\ell=q+(-q)=0$. This verifies cancellation of these two algebraic coefficients in that interface only; it does not identify them with a regulated anomaly, prove an all-orders theorem, or establish a nonperturbative gauge theory or cancellation of global anomalies.
items/ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation.md:44:[[def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface]]
items/ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation.md:52:[F1] [[def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface]]: with $\{A,B\}=AB+BA$, $d^{abc}=\sum_i\operatorname{tr}_{V_i}(T^a_{R_i}\{T^b_{R_i},T^c_{R_i}\})$; the separate linear representation coefficient is $\ell^a=\sum_i\operatorname{tr}_{V_i}(T^a_{R_i})$. These coefficient definitions do not construct a field model or assert an anomaly/descent identification.
items/ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation.md:60:2.1 The linear representation coefficient is $q+(-q)=0$. Thus both the cubic coefficient and the separately defined linear coefficient vanish by direct arithmetic. This calculation asserts no descent identification, loop theorem, global-anomaly conclusion, or nonperturbative existence claim. [given, A1, F1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎
items/prop-qftx-weight-anomaly-obstruction.md:2:id: prop-qftx-weight-anomaly-obstruction
items/prop-qftx-weight-anomaly-obstruction.md:4:title: "A nontrivial weight anomaly obstructs forgetting the weights"
items/prop-qftx-weight-anomaly-obstruction.md:47:Assume full AC and its inherited countable-choice consequences, and fix a weighted RT bordism $M$ with all its boundary data, ribbon graph, object Lagrangians, and coupons held fixed. If its integer weight is $n$, then $Z(M,n+1)=\kappa Z(M,n)$. If $\kappa\ne1$ and $Z(M,n)$ is a nonzero linear map, the weighted RT assignment cannot factor through the operation that forgets integer weights while keeping the same maps. This obstruction concerns ordinary forgetting of the weight; an anomaly-canceling enlargement or a different normalization requires separate data and is not asserted here.
