items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:60:Choose the local Lorenz gauge $\partial^\mu A_\mu=0$ with constant $\xi>0$, dimensional regularization $D=4-2\epsilon$, modified minimal subtraction of $1/\epsilon$ poles together with $-\gamma_E+\log(4\pi)$, and a finite engineering-dimension bound $d_*$. The allowed counterterms are integrated Lorentz-scalar finite-jet polynomials of ghost number zero and dimension at most $d_*$ in $A,c,\bar c,b$, their antifields, and their spacetime derivatives. The formal loop variable $\lambda$ is dimensionless; $\Gamma(\lambda)=\Gamma_0+\sum_{n\geq1}\lambda^n\Gamma_n$ is a formal coefficient sequence with no convergence at nonzero $\lambda$ asserted. Write $\Gamma^{(<n)}$ for a partial action whose coefficients below order $n$ already satisfy the Slavnov identity.
