items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:66:at every first failing order; put $\Xi_n=\Theta_n=0$ at nonfailing orders. Compact support or the model's boundary conditions make the integral of each $d_H$-exact four-form vanish. Then the counterterm series $C(\lambda)=-\sum_{n\geq1}\lambda^n\int_U\Xi_n$ yields $\mathfrak S(\Gamma(\lambda)+C(\lambda))=0$ coefficientwise.
items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:68:For $g\in\{0,1\}$, restrict $H^{g,4}(s\mid d_H)$, with $s=B_{\Gamma_0}$, to local cocycles of engineering dimension at most $d_*$; identify two allowed representatives when their difference is $sm+d_Hn$ for local forms of the indicated ghost numbers and the difference remains in the allowed power-counting space. The resulting ghost-number-zero quotient is exactly the local counterterm freedom modulo trivial counterterms and total derivatives. The ghost-number-one quotient classifies local obstruction classes in that space; a nonzero class cannot be removed by an allowed local counterterm. This is a quotient statement and asserts no finite basis of representatives. The conclusion is conditional on the local QAP and supplied anomaly-cancellation sequence; it proves neither premise and asserts no empirical result, continuum functional measure, convergence, or nonperturbative existence. Any finite-dimensional Faddeev–Popov Jacobian remains the ordinary Jacobian of its specified regulated group action and transverse slice; it is not a continuum functional determinant.
