items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:101:[A3] At every first failing order, an allowed local ghost-number-zero four-form $\Xi_n$ and ghost-number-one three-form $\Theta_n$ are supplied with $\delta_n=B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+d_H\Theta_n$. This is the explicit anomaly-cancellation hypothesis in the statement.
items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:118:2.2 By the supplied exactness sequence in the statement, write $\delta_n=B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n+d_H\Theta_n$ and set $\Gamma^{(<n+1)}:=\Gamma^{(<n)}-\lambda^n\int_U\Xi_n$. Bilinearity of the antibracket shows that the coefficient at order $n$ changes by $-B_{\Gamma_0}\Xi_n$; pairings with positive-loop terms and the quadratic counterterm term are $O(\lambda^{n+1})$. Thus the new defect is $\lambda^n\int_U d_H\Theta_n+O(\lambda^{n+1})$. [given, A3, F5, step 1.2, algebra]
items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:120:2.3 In the local-functional quotient of [F4], an allowed ghost-number-zero four-form is infinitesimally Slavnov-invariant precisely when its $s$-variation is a horizontal derivative. Two such changes are equivalent precisely when their difference is $sm+d_Hn$ in the stated power-counting space. These are exactly the cocycle and equivalence relations defining the restricted $H^{0,4}(s\mid d_H)$ in [F4]; applying the same definition at ghost number one gives the local obstruction quotient, whose nonzero classes cannot be represented by an allowed exact restoring counterterm. [given, F4, step 1.3, algebra]
items/pthm-qftx-perturbative-yang-mills-st-identity.md:122:3.1 The integral of the remaining $d_H$-exact term vanishes by the stated compact-support or boundary hypothesis, so the identity holds through order $n$. The supplied sequence defines a formal counterterm series, and induction over $n$ therefore yields $\mathfrak S(\Gamma(\lambda)+C(\lambda))=0$ coefficientwise, without a convergence assertion. [given, A3, A4, F1, step 2.2, algebra]

